# @TITLE@ channel

Describe what the `@KEY@` channel sends, to whom, and how an organization admin sets it up.

## 1. Set up the destination

Steps on the destination's own side, with screenshots (§C6.7 step 6).

## 2. Install the channel

`POST /api/v1/notification-channels/installations` with `"channel_key": "@KEY@"`. The settings
the form shows come from `GET /api/v1/notification-channels/@KEY@/schema`.

## 3. What data is sent

List every field that leaves AssetFlow, and which of them are personal data (they are sent only when
the installation allows personal data).

## 4. Failures

| Outcome | Result |
| --- | --- |
| timeout, connection error, 5xx | retried (3 attempts, 1 s then 4 s apart) |
| any 4xx | not retried: dead-lettered, admins are told |

See [dead-letter handling](../../operations/runbooks/dlq-handling.md).
